# State Machine Standards

## Reference Documentation

- `docs/lld/03-state-machines.md` - ALL state diagrams
- State machines MUST match the documented diagrams exactly

## State Transitions Are Code, Not Data

```java
// ✅ Enum-based state machine with explicit transitions
public enum ExecutionState {
    PENDING {
        @Override
        public ExecutionState onStart() { return RUNNING; }
        @Override
        public ExecutionState onCancel() { return CANCELLED; }
        @Override
        public ExecutionState onValidationFailed() { return FAILED; }
    },
    RUNNING {
        @Override
        public ExecutionState onAllJobsSucceeded() { return SUCCEEDED; }
        @Override
        public ExecutionState onAnyJobFailed() { return FAILED; }
        @Override
        public ExecutionState onCancel() { return CANCELLED; }
    },
    SUCCEEDED,  // Terminal
    FAILED {
        @Override
        public ExecutionState onRetry() { return RETRYING; }
    },
    CANCELLED,  // Terminal
    RETRYING {
        @Override
        public ExecutionState onStart() { return RUNNING; }
    };
    
    // Default: illegal transition
    public ExecutionState onStart() { throw illegalTransition("start"); }
    public ExecutionState onCancel() { throw illegalTransition("cancel"); }
    public ExecutionState onAllJobsSucceeded() { throw illegalTransition("allJobsSucceeded"); }
    public ExecutionState onAnyJobFailed() { throw illegalTransition("anyJobFailed"); }
    public ExecutionState onRetry() { throw illegalTransition("retry"); }
    public ExecutionState onValidationFailed() { throw illegalTransition("validationFailed"); }
    
    public boolean isTerminal() {
        return this == SUCCEEDED || this == FAILED || this == CANCELLED;
    }
    
    private IllegalStateException illegalTransition(String event) {
        return new IllegalStateException(
            "Cannot " + event + " from state " + this.name()
        );
    }
}
```

## Aggregate State Transitions

```java
// ✅ State changes happen through domain methods, not setters
public class Execution {
    private ExecutionState state = ExecutionState.PENDING;
    
    public void start() {
        state = state.onStart();  // Throws if invalid
        startedAt = Instant.now();
        publishEvent(new ExecutionStartedEvent(id, startedAt));
    }
    
    public void cancel(UserId cancelledBy) {
        state = state.onCancel();
        cancelledAt = Instant.now();
        this.cancelledBy = cancelledBy;
        publishEvent(new ExecutionCancelledEvent(id, cancelledBy, cancelledAt));
    }
    
    // ❌ NEVER expose setState
    // public void setState(ExecutionState state) - NO!
}
```

## Testing State Machines

```java
@Test
void execution_pendingToRunning_validTransition() {
    var execution = Execution.create(...);
    assertThat(execution.getState()).isEqualTo(PENDING);
    
    execution.start();
    
    assertThat(execution.getState()).isEqualTo(RUNNING);
    assertThat(execution.getStartedAt()).isNotNull();
}

@Test
void execution_succeededToRunning_throwsIllegalState() {
    var execution = Execution.create(...);
    execution.start();
    execution.complete(true);  // Now SUCCEEDED
    
    assertThatThrownBy(() -> execution.start())
        .isInstanceOf(IllegalStateException.class)
        .hasMessageContaining("Cannot start from state SUCCEEDED");
}

// ✅ Test ALL transitions documented in state diagram
@ParameterizedTest
@MethodSource("validTransitions")
void validTransitionsWork(ExecutionState from, String event, ExecutionState to) {
    // ...
}

@ParameterizedTest
@MethodSource("invalidTransitions")
void invalidTransitionsThrow(ExecutionState from, String event) {
    // ...
}
```

## State Machine Checklist

Before implementing any state machine:

- [ ] State diagram exists in `docs/lld/03-state-machines.md`
- [ ] All states are enum values
- [ ] All transitions are explicit methods
- [ ] Invalid transitions throw IllegalStateException
- [ ] Terminal states identified
- [ ] 100% transition coverage in tests
- [ ] Events published on state changes
